Done. `rename` is implemented in `rust/src/store.rs:18-44`.

**What it does:** reads the old `{old_id}.note` file, parses the 4 SEP-delimited fields (`id\n---\ntitle\n---\npinned\n---\nbody`), rewrites a new `{new_id}.note` with the new id and title while preserving `parts[2]` (pinned) and `parts[3]` (body, which carries the tags), then deletes the old file.

**Key points:**
- Only touches the old file by name (`{old_id}.note`) and writes the new one — no reliance on in-memory note lists, so it matches how `save`/`load_all` derive names from ids.
- Handles `old_id == new_id` (rewrites in place, no stray deletion) and returns an error if the old file is missing or malformed.
- After the call, `load_all` returns exactly one note with the new id/title and no old file remains on disk.

